From eef17eedc041682789545da622eba9f2a6743cb4 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: =?UTF-8?q?John=20T=C3=B6rnblom?= <john.tornblom@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 23 Oct 2026 22:14:47 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 03/12] util/disk_cache: shader cache support for the PS4

On the PS4 the cache folders and files are made accessible to other
users (e.g. the FTP service) whatever the umask. Modes are only changed
when needed, as metadata writes are slow there.

The mesa-db cache gets an exclusive mode, MESA_DISK_CACHE_DATABASE_EXCLUSIVE
(the default on the PS4): each part is opened and locked once for the
life of the process and shared by all its caches, access times are
written in batches, and a lookup no longer creates every part.

Co-authored-by: Mihawk <163614687+mihawk-99@users.noreply.github.com>
Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
